IMPORT prelude

-- Sewerage, Drainage and Coastal Protection Act 1999 (Singapore) -- what the Act asks of an owner, occupier, contractor or business
-- whose premises or works touch a sewer or a drain: keeping private sewers and drains in order (ss 10, 22A, 63), enquiring before
-- digging (s 13A), discharges into the public sewers (ss 16, 16A, 17, 18, 19), damage to sewers and drains (ss 20, 30, 67A), drains
-- and drainage reserves (ss 24, 24A), water intake works (s 31), notices and appeals (ss 9, 17, 22, 41, 42, 47), and the penalties
-- those sections set.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 1/7/2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/SDCPA1999.txt. The revised edition incorporates amendments up to 1 December 2021; later amendments
-- are annotated, the most frequent being Act 38 of 2024 (wef 01/03/2025) and Act 8 of 2026 (wef 29/05/2026, which added Part 4A on
-- coastal flooding); the latest date annotated is wef 01/07/2026.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0068 (subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl): Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a
-- sharper question yet. SCOPED to the duties, offences and appeals an owner, occupier, contractor or discharging business meets.
-- Not encoded: Part 4A (coastal flooding: prescribed places, coastal protection measures, ss 30A-30Q), the Board's construction and
-- vesting powers beyond the appeal against a vesting notice, s 11 approval procedure and ss 32-36 (codes of practice, qualified
-- persons), s 12 and s 15 notices, s 22B flood protection measures, s 23 and s 26 drainage works approvals, enforcement powers
-- (ss 38-46A), Part 7A compensation and owner-initiated acquisition, cost recovery (ss 48-60), composition (s 70), and the
-- regulations, codes and orders made under the Act (none was retrieved).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions of the example rows. No pipeline, no
-- coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Sewerage, Drainage and Coastal Protection Act 1999 -- sewers and drains`

§§ `10, 22A and 63 -- private sewers and drains are the owners' to keep in order`

-- s 10(1): "Every sewerage system at any premises (but not any public sewerage system) must be altered, repaired and kept in proper
-- order at the cost and expense of the owner of the premises." (1A): where it "(a) is connected to any other premises; and (b) serves
-- the sewerage needs of the other premises, then the owner of the other premises must also" keep it in order. (5): contravening (1)
-- or (1A) is an offence. s 22A(1), (2), (6) say the same of a stormwater drainage system or drain, except one "under the control or
-- supervision of the Board or maintained by the Board". Neither section sets a penalty, so s 63 applies: "a fine not exceeding $15,000
-- or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 months or ... both, and in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not
-- exceeding $500 for every day or part of a day during which the offence continues after conviction".
GIVEN `owns the premises where it is` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `owns other premises it is connected to` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `it serves those other premises` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `it is public or the Board's` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person must keep the sewer or drain in proper order` IF
        (NOT `it is public or the Board's`)
    AND (    `owns the premises where it is`
         OR  (`owns other premises it is connected to` AND `it serves those other premises`))

GIVEN `days continued after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 63 maximum fine` MEANS 15000 PLUS 500 TIMES `days continued after conviction`

§§ `13A -- enquire before you dig`

-- s 13A(1): any person who "digs, bores, trenches, grades, excavates, tunnels or breaks any ground with any mechanical equipment, tool
-- or explosive ... without first -- (a) obtaining from the Board the relevant drainage plan or sewerage plan ...; (b) carrying out
-- trial trenches to physically ascertain the location of any public sewerage system ...; and (c) complying with such other
-- requirements as the Board may specify" commits an offence: "a fine not exceeding $50,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not
-- exceeding 3 years or ... both". All three steps are required; missing any one is the offence.
GIVEN `breaks ground with equipment, a tool or explosive` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `first obtained the Board's plans` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `first dug trial trenches` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `first complied with the Board's other requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the excavation is an offence under s 13A` IF
        `breaks ground with equipment, a tool or explosive`
    AND (    (NOT `first obtained the Board's plans`)
         OR  (NOT `first dug trial trenches`)
         OR  (NOT `first complied with the Board's other requirements`))

§§ `16, 16A -- discharges into the public sewers`

-- s 16(1): no discharge of "any trade effluent into any public sewerage system or any drain-line or sewer connected to a public
-- sewerage system, except -- (a) with the prior written approval of the Board; and (b) in accordance with the conditions of that
-- approval (if any) and any regulations". (2): s 16 does not apply to a dangerous or hazardous substance, or effluent containing one --
-- s 16A governs that, in the same words. s 16(6): not guilty "if the person proves that -- (a) the discharge ... was made in an
-- emergency to avoid danger to life or property; and (b) the person informed the Board of the discharge in writing as soon as was
-- reasonably practicable". s 16A HAS NO SUCH DEFENCE. s 16A(6): a contravention that "causes -- (a) injury or death to any person;
-- (b) damage to any public sewerage system which renders the sewerage system inoperable; or (c) severe disruption to the process of
-- treating sewage or the process of water reclamation" is the heavier offence.
DECLARE Discharge HAS
    `into a public sewer or connected drain-line` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is trade effluent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `contains a dangerous or hazardous substance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `had the Board's prior written approval` IS A BOOLEAN
    `followed the approval conditions and regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made in an emergency to avoid danger to life or property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Board told in writing as soon as reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `caused injury, death, an inoperable sewer or severe disruption` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the discharge` IS A Discharge
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the discharge is authorised` IF
        `the discharge`'s `had the Board's prior written approval`
    AND `the discharge`'s `followed the approval conditions and regulations`

GIVEN `the discharge` IS A Discharge
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the discharge is an offence under s 16` IF
        `the discharge`'s `into a public sewer or connected drain-line`
    AND `the discharge`'s `is trade effluent`
    AND (NOT `the discharge`'s `contains a dangerous or hazardous substance`)
    AND (NOT `the discharge is authorised` `the discharge`)
    AND (NOT (`the discharge`'s `made in an emergency to avoid danger to life or property`
              AND `the discharge`'s `Board told in writing as soon as reasonably practicable`))

GIVEN `the discharge` IS A Discharge
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the discharge is an offence under s 16A` IF
        `the discharge`'s `into a public sewer or connected drain-line`
    AND `the discharge`'s `contains a dangerous or hazardous substance`
    AND (NOT `the discharge is authorised` `the discharge`)

-- s 16(3), (4) and s 16A(2), (3): where effluent has been discharged from premises, "it is presumed, until the contrary is proved, that
-- the occupier of the premises has discharged, or caused or permitted to be discharged" it, and the presumption "is not rebutted
-- unless the occupier ... proves that the occupier had taken all reasonable precautions and exercised due diligence".
GIVEN `it came from the occupier's premises` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the occupier proved all reasonable precautions and due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the occupier is taken to have discharged it` IF
    `it came from the occupier's premises` AND (NOT `the occupier proved all reasonable precautions and due diligence`)

§§ `20, 30 and 67A -- damage`

-- s 20(1): causing damage to any public sewerage system, connected drain-line or sewer, or earth retaining structure: $50,000 or 3
-- months (first), $100,000 or 3 months (subsequent). s 20(2): "(a) does any act which renders any public sewerage system ... dangerous
-- or injurious to health; (b) causes any damage to a pipe of 0.9 metres or greater in diameter ...; or (c) does any act which disrupts
-- the operation of or causes damage to any sewage treatment plant, sewage treatment works or water reclamation facility": $200,000 or
-- 2 years (first), $400,000 or 2 years (subsequent).
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `not keeping a private sewer or drain in order (ss 10, 22A, 63)`
    `excavating without first enquiring (s 13A)`
    `unapproved sewerage or sanitary works (s 11)`
    `works near a sewer without approval (s 14)`
    `trade effluent without approval (s 16)`
    `hazardous discharge (s 16A(5))`
    `hazardous discharge causing harm (s 16A(6))`
    `ignoring an order to stop a hazardous discharge (s 17(4))`
    `discharging from a vehicle or through a manhole (s 18)`
    `putting building materials into a sewer (s 19)`
    `damaging the public sewerage system (s 20(1))`
    `serious damage to the sewerage system (s 20(2))`
    `obstructing a drain or drainage reserve (s 24)`
    `ignoring a tree notice (s 24A)`
    `damaging a stormwater drain (s 30)`
    `unapproved water intake works (s 31)`
    `not complying with a notice (s 41)`

GIVEN `the discharge` IS A Discharge
GIVETH AN Offence
`the hazardous discharge offence` MEANS
    IF `the discharge`'s `caused injury, death, an inoperable sewer or severe disruption`
    THEN `hazardous discharge causing harm (s 16A(6))`
    ELSE `hazardous discharge (s 16A(5))`

GIVEN `pipe diameter in metres` IS A NUMBER,
      `disrupted or damaged a treatment plant or water reclamation facility` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `made the system dangerous or injurious to health` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Offence
`the sewer damage offence` MEANS
    IF     `pipe diameter in metres` AT LEAST 0.9
        OR `disrupted or damaged a treatment plant or water reclamation facility`
        OR `made the system dangerous or injurious to health`
    THEN `serious damage to the sewerage system (s 20(2))`
    ELSE `damaging the public sewerage system (s 20(1))`

-- s 20(3): "it is a defence ... to prove that the person took all reasonable precautions and exercised all due diligence to avoid the
-- commission of the offence, but this defence is not available to a person who may be liable by virtue of section 67A".
-- s 67A: where an offence is committed by an agent or employee, the principal or employer is liable "in the same manner and to the
-- same extent ... unless that other person proves ... that the offence was committed without that other person's consent or
-- connivance and that it was not attributable to any neglect on that other person's part".
GIVEN `liable only through s 67A` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved all reasonable precautions and due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 20 due-diligence defence succeeds` IF
    `proved all reasonable precautions and due diligence` AND (NOT `liable only through s 67A`)

GIVEN `an agent or employee committed it in the work` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the principal proved no consent or connivance` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the principal proved no neglect of its own` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the principal is liable under s 67A` IF
        `an agent or employee committed it in the work`
    AND (NOT (`the principal proved no consent or connivance` AND `the principal proved no neglect of its own`))

§§ `Penalties`

-- The maxima, minima and "further fine" per day after conviction, from the sections cited in each name. "Repeat" means a second or
-- subsequent conviction where the section distinguishes it. 0 months means the section provides no imprisonment; 0 minimum means the
-- section sets none. s 17(4) gives "a further fine of $2,000" a day, not "not exceeding" $2,000. s 31(5) says "a fine not exceeding
-- $20,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 months" -- without "or to both".
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `repeat` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `not keeping a private sewer or drain in order (ss 10, 22A, 63)` THEN 15000
    WHEN `excavating without first enquiring (s 13A)` THEN 50000
    WHEN `unapproved sewerage or sanitary works (s 11)` THEN IF `repeat` THEN 100000 ELSE 50000
    WHEN `works near a sewer without approval (s 14)` THEN 20000
    WHEN `trade effluent without approval (s 16)` THEN IF `repeat` THEN 50000 ELSE 20000
    WHEN `hazardous discharge (s 16A(5))` THEN IF `repeat` THEN 100000 ELSE 50000
    WHEN `hazardous discharge causing harm (s 16A(6))` THEN IF `repeat` THEN 400000 ELSE 200000
    WHEN `ignoring an order to stop a hazardous discharge (s 17(4))` THEN 100000
    WHEN `discharging from a vehicle or through a manhole (s 18)` THEN 20000
    WHEN `putting building materials into a sewer (s 19)` THEN 20000
    WHEN `damaging the public sewerage system (s 20(1))` THEN IF `repeat` THEN 100000 ELSE 50000
    WHEN `serious damage to the sewerage system (s 20(2))` THEN IF `repeat` THEN 400000 ELSE 200000
    WHEN `obstructing a drain or drainage reserve (s 24)` THEN IF `repeat` THEN 100000 ELSE 50000
    WHEN `ignoring a tree notice (s 24A)` THEN 10000
    WHEN `damaging a stormwater drain (s 30)` THEN IF `repeat` THEN 100000 ELSE 50000
    WHEN `unapproved water intake works (s 31)` THEN 20000
    WHEN `not complying with a notice (s 41)` THEN 20000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `repeat` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `trade effluent without approval (s 16)` THEN IF `repeat` THEN 10000 ELSE 4000
    WHEN `hazardous discharge (s 16A(5))` THEN IF `repeat` THEN 20000 ELSE 10000
    WHEN `hazardous discharge causing harm (s 16A(6))` THEN IF `repeat` THEN 80000 ELSE 40000
    WHEN `ignoring an order to stop a hazardous discharge (s 17(4))` THEN 20000
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `not keeping a private sewer or drain in order (ss 10, 22A, 63)` THEN 3
    WHEN `excavating without first enquiring (s 13A)` THEN 36
    WHEN `trade effluent without approval (s 16)` THEN 3
    WHEN `hazardous discharge (s 16A(5))` THEN 12
    WHEN `hazardous discharge causing harm (s 16A(6))` THEN 24
    WHEN `ignoring an order to stop a hazardous discharge (s 17(4))` THEN 3
    WHEN `damaging the public sewerage system (s 20(1))` THEN 3
    WHEN `serious damage to the sewerage system (s 20(2))` THEN 24
    WHEN `damaging a stormwater drain (s 30)` THEN 3
    WHEN `unapproved water intake works (s 31)` THEN 3
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `fine and imprisonment may both be imposed` IF
        `the maximum imprisonment in months` `the offence` GREATER THAN 0
    AND (NOT (`the offence` EQUALS `unapproved water intake works (s 31)`))

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `repeat` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the further fine per day after conviction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `not keeping a private sewer or drain in order (ss 10, 22A, 63)` THEN 500
    WHEN `trade effluent without approval (s 16)` THEN IF `repeat` THEN 2000 ELSE 1000
    WHEN `hazardous discharge (s 16A(5))` THEN 2000
    WHEN `ignoring an order to stop a hazardous discharge (s 17(4))` THEN 2000
    OTHERWISE 0

§§ `24, 24A -- drains and drainage reserves`

-- s 24(1): no "(a) ... fence, partition, structure or object in, above or across, or enclosing ... any drain or reservoir; (b) ...
-- obstruction to the flow of any stormwater drainage system; or (c) ... within any drainage reserve any fence, retaining wall,
-- foundation, manhole, pipe, cable, mains or any obstruction or structure (whether temporary or permanent)" without a clearance
-- certificate or approval under s 33. (1A): not "except with the prior approval of the Board -- (a) deposit or leave any soil, building
-- material or components, construction or renovation debris ... within any drain or drainage reserve; (b) park or leave any vehicle on
-- any drainage reserve; (c) clear, dig up or cultivate, or interfere with any substance on, in or forming part of, any drain or
-- drainage reserve". (4): $50,000 first, $100,000 subsequent. Walking along a reserve or gardening wholly on one's own land is not in
-- the list (an inference from the list, not a statement in the text).
DECLARE Activity IS ONE OF
    `parking a car on a drainage reserve`
    `leaving renovation debris in a drain`
    `putting up a fence across a drain`
    `laying a cable in a drainage reserve`
    `growing vegetables on a drainage reserve`
    `walking along a drainage reserve`
    `gardening in one's own back garden`

GIVEN `the activity` IS AN Activity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the activity needs the Board's clearance or approval` IF
    CONSIDER `the activity`
    WHEN `walking along a drainage reserve` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `gardening in one's own back garden` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the activity` IS AN Activity, `approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the activity is an offence under s 24` IF
    `the activity needs the Board's clearance or approval` `the activity` AND (NOT `approved`)

-- s 24A(1): where a tree or plant "on any premises adjoining a drainage reserve" is likely to obstruct or hinder a drain, "the Board
-- may serve a notice requiring the OCCUPIER of the premises to take any measures (including cutting the tree or plant ...)". (2):
-- failing to comply "without reasonable excuse" -- a fine not exceeding $10,000.
DECLARE Party IS ONE OF
    `the occupier of the adjoining premises`
    `a landlord who does not occupy them`

GIVEN `the party` IS A Party
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the tree notice is addressed to the party` IF
    `the party` EQUALS `the occupier of the adjoining premises`

GIVEN `served with a tree notice` IS A BOOLEAN, `complied` IS A BOOLEAN, `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the failure is an offence under s 24A` IF
    `served with a tree notice` AND (NOT `complied`) AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`)

§§ `41 -- failing to comply with a notice`

-- s 41(1): where a person served with a notice under (among others) s 10, 11, 14, 20, 22A, 24 or 30 "fails to comply with the notice
-- within the time specified ... (a) the person shall, unless the person satisfies the court that the person has used all due diligence
-- to comply with the notice, be guilty of an offence" -- a fine not exceeding $20,000; and (b) an authorised officer may enter and
-- execute the works. (1A): the officer may do so "whether or not any proceedings have been started, or any conviction has been
-- obtained".
GIVEN `complied in time` IS A BOOLEAN, `satisfied the court of all due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits the s 41 offence` IF
    (NOT `complied in time`) AND (NOT `satisfied the court of all due diligence`)

§§ `9, 17, 22, 42 and 47 -- appeals to the Minister`

-- s 9(3), 22(3): an owner aggrieved by notice of the Board's intention to vest a private sewer or drain in the Government "may appeal
-- to the Minister within 28 days"; (5): the Board may proceed only if no appeal is filed in time or it is dismissed.
-- s 17(2): an order to stop a hazardous discharge -- appeal "within 14 days"; (3): "an aggrieved person must comply with the order
-- pending the outcome of the appeal". s 47(4)(c) excludes s 17 orders from s 47.
-- s 42(1): a notice mentioned in s 41 (but not one under s 30E(8) or 30G(7)) -- appeal "within 14 days"; (1)(b)(ii): until the appeal
-- is decided or abandoned "the notice is suspended and need not be complied with" (though (3) lets the Minister authorise immediate
-- work in stated cases).
-- s 47(1): any other notice, order, direction or authorisation -- 14 days; a declaration -- 28 days; (2) suspended meanwhile. (4)(d)
-- excludes notices under (among others) ss 10, 24, 30, 30E. s 24A is in neither the s 41 list nor the s 47(4) exclusions, so a tree
-- notice falls under s 47.
-- A s 30E(8) coastal protection notice is excluded from s 42 by its own words and from s 47 by (4)(d); no other appeal for it was
-- found in the Act (an inference from searching the deposit, not a statement in it).
DECLARE Instrument IS ONE OF
    `a notice of intention to vest a private sewer or drain (ss 9, 22)`
    `an order to stop a hazardous discharge (s 17)`
    `a notice to repair a private sewer (s 10)`
    `a notice to remove an obstruction from a drain (s 24)`
    `a tree notice (s 24A)`
    `a declaration by the Board within s 47`
    `a coastal protection notice (s 30E(8))`

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the appeal period in days` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the instrument`
    WHEN `a notice of intention to vest a private sewer or drain (ss 9, 22)` THEN 28
    WHEN `a declaration by the Board within s 47` THEN 28
    WHEN `a coastal protection notice (s 30E(8))` THEN 0
    OTHERWISE 14

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an appeal to the Minister lies` IF
    `the appeal period in days` `the instrument` GREATER THAN 0

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it must be obeyed while the appeal is pending` IF
    `the instrument` EQUALS `an order to stop a hazardous discharge (s 17)`

§§ `31 -- water intake works`

-- s 31(1): "A person must not, without the approval of the Board, construct any works for taking or intercepting water from any place
-- or sea, within the territorial limits of Singapore." (6): "This section does not apply to the lands, buildings and installations of
-- the Board."
GIVEN `constructs works to take or intercept water in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `approved` IS A BOOLEAN, `on the Board's own land` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the works contravene s 31` IF
    `constructs works to take or intercept water in Singapore` AND (NOT `approved`) AND (NOT `on the Board's own land`)
